Plan:
Fix two issues in pluggy:

1. In `src/pluggy/_hooks.py`, modify `HookCaller._remove_plugin` to remove *all* hook implementations belonging to the given plugin, not just the first. Change the loop to collect indices of all matching implementations and delete them in reverse order (or use a list comprehension to rebuild the list). Keep raising `ValueError` if none are found.

2. In `src/pluggy/_manager.py`, modify `PluginManager.get_hookcallers` to avoid duplicate hookcaller entries when a plugin has multiple implementations on the same hook. Change the inner loop to break after the first match per hookcaller (or use `any()`).

Verification: run `python -m pytest testing` to ensure all tests pass, especially any tests covering plugin unregistration and `get_hookcallers`.

